    "body": "## Security impact\n\n`GET /disputes/{id}` is authenticated, but previously an unrelated user received `403 Forbidden` for an existing dispute while a nonexistent ID returned `404`. Because dispute IDs are numeric, this allowed authenticated outsiders to enumerate which sensitive disputes exist.\n\n## Fix\n\n- keep full dispute detail access for the requester, assigned worker, and admins;\n- return the existing neutral `ResourceNotFoundException` for authenticated outsiders;\n- leave mutation authorization semantics unchanged;\n- add focused regression coverage for outsider, participant, and admin reads.\n\n## Scope\n\nPrivacy/authorization hardening only; no schema or financial-flow changes.",
